events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:a21de4ab9b8869e8ff15a07ef35b34efc41cb80781674205ed5408d2e1b60f80","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-22T02:04:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-22T02:04:08Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m148-v0.14.8/m14stage8-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m148-v0.14.8","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m148-v0.14.8","body":"# Engacer OS M14.8 - Original x64 EXE installer lifecycle\n\nM14.8 native/source/media qualification passes: 105 native and 41 supporting host groups across 147 campaign tasks, including actual VMware installation and two independent starts. Original SumatraPDF 3.6.1 x64 EXE GUI installation, cold removal and cold reinstall pass. Both installation cycles verify four original payloads and two actual shortcuts. The PDF reader itself remains unqualified. Previous 7-Zip and Notepad++ MSI scopes are retained. Build fdb650a0e4cff632bd4945cc1b024567 binds compiled source bd12730bf19eee5a4ab496d798a7c0435728fed0 and 825 exact inputs. Public download and independent content verification are separate delivery gates; current status records their result. Native homepage Save is blocked by the reproduced BrixCanvas website-read error; article synchronization works. A stale homepage is not counted as successful publication.\n\n## What changes\n\nWindows Apps reviews MSI and EXE sources without running their custom actions.\nThe M14.8 EXE broker runs the pinned original SumatraPDF 3.6.1 x64 installer\nand uninstaller through Engacer OS's own kernel and Windows compatibility APIs.\nThe application instructions execute natively; VMware is the external test\nhost, not an embedded Windows guest. The installer and vendor DLLs are unchanged.\n\nThe confirmed operation grants access to its own product folder, two approved\nshortcuts, scoped per-user registrations and a private temporary namespace.\nProduct ownership is protected outside that folder. Completion requires real\nchild exit, independent payload and shortcut verification, and durable state.\nThe original uninstaller's self-copy helper and limited command batch perform\nreal cleanup. Unrelated documents and the source download are preserved. Changed\nor extra product files refuse destructive removal before the original recursive\nuninstaller can erase them.\n\nThe production-media chain verifies installation, a cold original removal and\na cold reinstall. Both installation cycles independently hash four original\npayloads and parse both actual shortcuts through the Windows-native link reader.\nThe earlier original 7-Zip and Notepad++ MSI lifecycle scope is retained.\n\n## Test scope and corrections\n\nAll 147 campaign tasks pass: 105 native groups, 41 supporting host\ngroups and the matching VMware starter. These include BIOS/UEFI ISO/USB\ninstallation, independent disk starts, ordinary/compact/4K paths, repeated GUI\nfault containment and actual enabled-device VMware installation and starts.\nFinal evidence records the completed result rather than inferring it from a\nsuccessful build or a selected application.\n\nA real integrated snapshot/mapping handle collision was corrected with separate\nhandle domains and native coexistence tests. The rejected candidate is preserved.\nTwo owned historical paint/fault probes now compare selected-font API metrics\ninstead of assuming a fixed 16-pixel height; their 21 lifecycle/fault repetitions,\npixel checks and zero-retention requirements remain. Original vendor bodies and\nhistorical accepted sources are not edited. A final generation guard also rejected 99 obsolete refusal keys; both the\nexact generated table and diagnostic inventory were corrected before rebuilding\nand rerunning the full campaign. One initial 4K control observation\nrefused; its unchanged repeat passed. No cause or OS fix is inferred from that\nrepeat.\n\n## Resource measurements and limits\n\nThe measured final-media EXE install, removal and reinstall respectively peak at\n7611, 3666 and 7611 native managed pages. Measured retained page deltas are 1, 5 and 1.\nThe session UI cache accounts for one retained page; four additional retained\nallocator pages in the removal measurement are not attributed. These are bounded\ntask observations, not total OS RAM, a zero-retention claim or a Windows speed\ncomparison. Configured VM RAM, framebuffer, fixed load and caches are separate.\nWhole-system CPU/RAM/storage optimization remains the M14.16 release gate.\n\nThe PDF reader itself, preview/filter operation, arbitrary EXE installers, general\nMSI packages, Notepad++ editor use, Firefox execution and universal Windows x64\ncompatibility remain unqualified. Close the finished original installer using\nits title-bar X; its Start SumatraPDF action is not a qualified reader launch.\nInterrupted EXE records can be inspected; automatic EXE rollback is not offered.\n\nCanonical fonts provide actual metrics and bounded drawing, but the original\ndecorative SumatraPDF logo is clipped with the fallback font. This is not\npixel-identical Windows rendering.\n\nThe approved future platform plan is M14.9-M14.16, not a fixture whitelist.\nAfter M14.8, work stops before M14.9 as requested. BrixCanvas platform findings\nremain in the combined report. The native homepage Save error is recorded\nseparately from the working GitHub-driven article publisher; a stale homepage\nis not counted as successful publication.\n\n## Guides and evidence\n\n- [Install and restart in VMware](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/handbook/install-m148.md)\n- [First day](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/handbook/first-day-m148.md)\n- [MSI and original EXE installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/handbook/windows-m148.md)\n- [Stage gates](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/milestones/m14-8.md)\n- [Architecture and bounds](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/architecture/installers-m148.md)\n- [Approved M14.9-M14.16 plan](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/milestones/m14-consolidated.md)\n- [Current delivery status](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/docs/roadmap/status.md)\n\n## Matching media and evidence\n\n- EngacerOS-M14STAGE8.iso SHA-256: 318ab2f69513eb11e5c2878a31db3703f4b7ee11ce2db6ea6234015f0b3fcc54\n- EngacerOS-M14STAGE8-VMware.zip SHA-256: df420bc10fc6d12c01ad6d50c89d8bec55aa17324cf361cb3cf6878649eac786\n- [Native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/evidence/M14/8/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/evidence/M14/8/resources.json), [visual review](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/98f1aaebb912a6f80b8d205a929d611f1fadce70/evidence/M14/8/visual-review.json).\n"}